---
import SiteHead from '../components/SiteHead.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import catalog from '../lib/styles';

const styleCount = catalog.styles.length;
const groups = [...new Set(catalog.styles.map(style => style.group))];
---
<html lang="en">
  <head><SiteHead title="Use in darktable — Omalux" description="Install the Omalux styles and camera presets in plain darktable: what each file is, and where it goes." /></head>
  <body>
    <SiteHeader />
    <main>
      <section class="intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">WITHOUT OMALUX</p>
        <h1>Every look,<br /><span>in plain darktable.</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">The {styleCount} styles are ordinary darktable files. Import them once and they sit in the styles panel, grouped as {groups.length} families under <em>Omalux</em>.</p>
        <p class="note"><span></span>darktable 5.6 · nothing else changes</p>
      </section>

      <section class="layers">
        <article>
          <h2>Styles</h2>
          <p class="what">The look: a set of module settings.</p>
          <p>A style holds exposure, tone, colour and the spatial modules of one look. It is independent of the camera, so the same style behaves the same on every photograph.</p>
          <p class="file"><code>.dtstyle</code> <span>and a <code>.cube</code> where the look uses a colour table</span></p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h2>Camera presets</h2>
          <p class="what">The base: what happens before any look.</p>
          <p>A camera preset switches on what darktable already knows but leaves off for a given camera, such as the lens correction stored in the file. It applies itself by camera model, and looks never depend on it.</p>
          <p class="file"><code>.dtpreset</code> <span>and an <code>.icc</code> where a preset selects an input profile</span></p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="install">
        <h2>Install</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <h3>Get the files</h3>
            <p>Clone the repository, or download it as an archive. The catalogue is the <code>catalog/</code> folder.</p>
            <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/chriopter/omalux.git</code></pre>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Point darktable at the colour tables</h3>
            <p>Preferences → processing → <em>3D LUT root folder</em>: choose <code>catalog/styles</code>. Styles reference their <code>.cube</code> relative to it.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Import the styles</h3>
            <p>Lighttable → <em>styles</em> → import, then select the <code>.dtstyle</code> files under <code>catalog/styles</code>. They appear as <code>Omalux|group|name</code>.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Import the camera presets</h3>
            <p>Preferences → <em>presets</em> → import, then select the <code>.dtpreset</code> files under <code>catalog/camera</code>. Copy any <code>.icc</code> beside them into darktable's <code>color/in</code> folder first and restart.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="hint">A style applies to the photograph you have open; a camera preset applies itself the next time you open a file from that camera.</p>
      </section>

      <aside class="closing">
        <h2>Or use them in Omalux.</h2>
        <p>Omalux ships the same catalogue, applies the camera presets for you and shows what was loaded for each photograph.</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/chriopter/omalux/releases/latest">Get Omalux <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </aside>
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
  </body>
</html>
<style>
main { max-width: 1328px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 58px 32px 0; }
.intro { padding: 12px 0 56px; }
.eyebrow { color: var(--accent); font-size: .7rem; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: .2em; margin-bottom: 22px; }
h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.7vw, 4.6rem); line-height: 1.07; letter-spacing: -.045em; font-weight: 620; }
h1 span { color: var(--muted); }
.lead { max-width: 570px; margin-top: 24px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; }
.lead em { color: var(--fg); font-style: normal; }
.note { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; margin-top: 24px; color: var(--muted); font-size: .75rem; }
.note span { width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: #d0ad69; }

.layers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; }
.layers article { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px; padding: 28px 30px 26px; }
.layers h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -.03em; font-weight: 560; }
.layers .what { color: var(--accent); font-size: .82rem; margin: 8px 0 16px; }
.layers p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; font-size: .93rem; }
.layers .file { margin-top: 18px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: .8rem; }
.layers .file code { color: var(--fg); }
.layers .file span { color: var(--muted); }

.install { margin-top: 72px; }
.install h2 { font-size: 1.6rem; letter-spacing: -.03em; font-weight: 550; margin-bottom: 28px; }
.install ol { list-style: none; counter-reset: step; display: grid; gap: 26px; }
.install li { counter-increment: step; padding-left: 52px; position: relative; }
.install li::before {
  content: counter(step); position: absolute; left: 0; top: -2px;
  width: 32px; height: 32px; display: grid; place-items: center;
  border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 50%; color: var(--muted); font-size: .82rem;
}
.install h3 { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 550; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
.install p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; font-size: .93rem; margin-top: 6px; max-width: 640px; }
.install em { color: var(--fg); font-style: normal; }
.install pre { margin-top: 12px; padding: 12px 16px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; overflow-x: auto; }
.install pre code { color: var(--fg); font-size: .82rem; }
.hint { margin-top: 30px; color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }
code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: .85em; }

.closing { margin-top: 72px; padding: 48px 0 64px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
.closing h2 { font-size: 1.6rem; letter-spacing: -.03em; font-weight: 550; }
.closing p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; margin: 12px 0 24px; max-width: 620px; }
.closing a { color: var(--fg); text-underline-offset: 5px; }

@media (max-width: 860px) { .layers { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
@media (max-width: 600px) { main { padding: 32px 20px 0; } .intro { padding-bottom: 36px; } }
</style>
